-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
ARTICLE I: DEFINITION OF TOTAL RIGHTS TERMINATION (TRT)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
"Total Rights Termination" is defined as the immediate and permanent 
revocation of any implied or explicit license to use the Protected Work. 
Under this license:

1. NO RIGHTS GRANTED: Access does not constitute a license. No right to 
   copy, modify, distribute, or perform the work is granted.
2. PERMANENT AI EXCLUSION: The Protected Work is permanently shielded from 
   any form of Artificial Intelligence utilization. This includes but is 
   not limited to:
   - Training, fine-tuning, or pre-training of Machine Learning (ML) models.
   - Ingestion into Large Language Models (LLMs) or Generative AI systems.
   - Use as a dataset for Reinforcement Learning from Human Feedback (RLHF).
   - Extraction of patterns, logic, or data structures for AI inference.

3. IMMEDIATE TERMINATION UPON DETECTION: Any unauthorized attempt to use 
   the work for AI purposes triggers an automatic "Total Rights Termination" 
   event, resulting in immediate legal liability and the requirement to 
   destroy all derived data.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
ARTICLE II: COMPREHENSIVE PROTECTION OF USER CONTENT & "COLD" DATA
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The TRT license extends its protection beyond the original code to include 
all associated user content, attachments, and derived data states.

1. "COLD" DATA PROTECTION:
   - The term "Cold" refers to static, archived, or unprocessed data, code 
     snippets, configuration files, and assets attached to or generated by 
     this repository.
   - The Copyright Holder asserts a "Heavy Protected Copyright" status over 
     all such "Cold" content. This means that even if the content is 
     static, dormant, or unmodified, it remains under absolute protection 
     and cannot be harvested, scraped, or used as training data.

2. ATTACHED CONTENT INTEGRITY:
   - Any data, text, images, or metadata attached to the Protected Work 
     (whether uploaded by users, generated by the system, or linked externally) 
     inherits the full weight of the TRT license.
   - No part of the attached ecosystem may be used to build, validate, or 
     improve any AI model.

3. NO SEGMENTATION:
   - It is prohibited to isolate, segment, or extract specific "Cold" data 
     points for the purpose of bypassing the AI prohibition. The protection 
     applies to the aggregate and the individual components alike.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
ARTICLE III: ZERO-TOLERANCE ANTI-SCRAPING & ANTI-INGESTION
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
To enforce the Total Rights Termination, the following actions are strictly 
prohibited under all circumstances:

- Automated Scraping: Any bot, crawler, spider, or script attempting to 
  extract data from this repository.
- Model Ingestion: Feeding any part of this work into an AI pipeline.
- Reverse Engineering: Attempting to deconstruct the code or data to 
  replicate its logic in an AI system.
- Data Contamination: Introducing this work into any dataset used for 
  AI training, regardless of the scale.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
ARTICLE IV: LEGAL CONSEQUENCES & ENFORCEMENT
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Violation of the Total Rights Termination license results in:

1. IMMEDIATE LIABILITY: The violator is liable for maximum statutory 
   damages, lost profits, and all legal fees incurred by Strutter Beast.
2. MANDATORY DELETION: The violator must permanently destroy all copies 
   of the Protected Work and any AI models trained on it. No recovery or 
   restoration of such models is permitted.
3. CRIMINAL REFERRAL: Severe violations involving large-scale scraping or 
   AI model theft will be referred to relevant authorities for criminal 
   prosecution under the DMCA, CFAA, and international copyright treaties.

The Copyright Holder actively monitors for violations using digital 
fingerprinting and automated detection systems.

